l bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nAlpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency with Respiratory Manifestations vs Primary Humoral Immunodeficiency (IgA Deficiency / IgG Subclass Deficiencies):\n  Favours first:  chronic bronchitis, chronic pulmonary obstruction, dyspnea, emphysema, hepatic failure\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nAlpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency with Respiratory Manifestations vs Combined T-Cell and B-Cell Immunodeficiency (e.g., Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Variants):\n  Favours first:  chronic bronchitis, chronic pulmonary obstruction, cirrhosis, dyspnea, elevated hepatic transaminase\n  Favours second: abnormality of humoral immunity, abnormality of pelvic girdle bone morphology, absence of lymph node germinal center, absent specific antibody response, absent tonsils\n\nAlpha-1 Antitrypsin Deficiency with Respiratory Manifestations vs Phagocytic Cell Defects (e.g., Chronic Granulomatous Disease):\n  Favours first:  chronic bronchitis, chronic pulmonary obstruction, dyspnea, emphysema, hepatic failure\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nPrimary Humoral Immunodeficiency (IgA Deficiency / IgG Subclass Deficiencies) vs Combined T-Cell and B-Cell Immunodeficiency (e.g., Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Variants):\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abnormality of humoral immunity, abnormality of pelvic girdle bone morphology, absence of lymph node germinal center, absent specific antibody response, absent tonsils\n\nCombined T-Cell and B-Cell Immunodeficiency (e.g., Severe Combined Immunodeficiency Variants) vs Phagocytic Cell Defects (e.g., Chronic Granulomatous Disease):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of humoral immunity, abnormality of